    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Here is a draft to get you started on a professional and assertive tone.\n\n\"I am writing to respectfully express my strong concerns regarding the proposed new sex education curriculum. I believe that the ultimate authority in defining the values and sensitive topics for our children should reside with the parents, not solely the school board. We strongly advocate for a policy that prioritizes and actively involves parental consent in all aspects of the curriculum for these important subject matters. I urge the board to ensure that strong, definitive rights for local families are central to this decision-making process for the good of our community's children.\"",
